  "_comment": "Illustrative ADR-BCP-018 instances for the first-party Nabhold Group Africa structure, corrected to ADR-BCP-026 (sections 3, 5) and ADR-BCP-027 (sections 1.1, 4.2, 11). Runtime authority is the Control Plane; these are examples, not runtime data. A Shared first-party registry entry is governed identity and declared intent, never verification: every Organisation and LegalEntityProfile here is UNVERIFIED with source_authority shared-first-party-identity, matching what the Control Plane first-party reconciler records. NABHOLD and THAMANI-GLOBAL are REGISTERED_EVIDENCED in contracts/legal-entity/registry.yaml (CIPC COR 14.3 certificates, reviewer sign-off pending): their profiles carry the jurisdiction, the registration identifier (verified:false) and the registry's legal_evidence_ref, and become VERIFIED only through independent Control Plane review of that evidence. ZURIBEANS and EQUATOR-ESTATE are declared NOT_INCORPORATED operating businesses: UNINCORPORATED_ORGANISATION records with no LegalEntityProfile, no jurisdiction and no registration identifier; they trade only through Nabhold as scoped legal actor under an independently approved OperatingLegalActorMandate. Incorporation dates, legal status and ownership percentages are not recorded in the registry and are omitted or UNKNOWN rather than invented. The Nabhold OWNS relationship to Thamani Global, the CONTROLS relationships to the two unincorporated businesses (sponsorship; no ownership is asserted because nothing is incorporated to own) and the PLATFORM_* relationships are PENDING_REVIEW: the registry records group roles but not company-secretarial ownership evidence, so ADR-BCP-017 INTERNAL eligibility must fail closed until the corporate relationship is independently verified. Canonical entity ids here are readable illustrations; runtime ids are Control Plane-minted.",
